dev_full_dump.pgdump filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# #3055: build-journal/<id>.md are per-issue, one-writer-per-file, append-only
# session bookends. Independent agent sessions each ADD their own file, and the
# dev-server coordinator (scripts/dev-server/) merges those agent-branch commits
# into the shared C:\dev-server checkout one at a time. Two branches that carry
# divergent histories for the SAME build-journal/<id>.md path therefore produce a
# `CONFLICT (add/add)` on merge -- the exact recurring failure #2830 patched by
# hand for two specific files and #3055 hit again for another. The content of a
# build-journal file inside the dev-server checkout is throwaway documentation
# (the authoritative bookend history lives on origin/main), so a lossless union
# is always a safe automatic resolution. `merge=union` makes git resolve both
# add/add and modify/modify on these paths by taking lines from both sides with
# no conflict markers, so the coordinator's merge-back never stalls on a bookend
# again. (Belt-and-suspenders: scripts/dev-server/git.mjs also resolves a merge
# whose conflicts are confined to these paths in code, covering any checkout that
# has not yet picked up this attribute.)
build-journal/*.md merge=union

# #2938: shebang + CRLF makes a .mjs file un-importable from vitest/Vite on
# Windows -- a bare "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" that blames the
# wrong (importing) file, not the actual broken module. node --check and a
# direct CLI run both pass; only a vitest/Vite-transformed import ever sees
# it. Force LF on .mjs repo-wide so a Windows checkout/rebase can never
# reintroduce CRLF into one of these files again.
*.mjs text eol=lf
